{
  "case_id": "2009-08-1107",
  "document_hash": "b7e294161f418f27706ae8c5baec0cd128fbba91ea099c85a350a6bee97a05f2",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1107",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b7e294161f418f27706ae8c5baec0cd128fbba91ea099c85a350a6bee97a05f2",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b7e294161f41-0000-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The diversity statute deems a corporation a citizen of, quote, \"the State where it has its principal place of business,\" closed quote. The Ninth Circuit erred in holding that Petitioner Hertz is a citizen of California, even though Hertz is headquartered in New Jersey and conducts over 80 percent of its operations outside the State of California, and even though, under the court's approach, national corporations could regularly be deemed California citizens if they conduct operations in that State that are proportional to the State's population."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1107",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b7e294161f418f27706ae8c5baec0cd128fbba91ea099c85a350a6bee97a05f2",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b7e294161f41-0000-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "First, the strong preference for simplicity and ease of administration in jurisdictional rules; and second, Congress's purposes in 1958 to preserve diversity jurisdiction for corporations in 48 States and to deny access to diversity jurisdiction only in one State, the State where the corporation had its home or principal place of business."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1107",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b7e294161f418f27706ae8c5baec0cd128fbba91ea099c85a350a6bee97a05f2",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b7e294161f41-0000-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Counsel, the problem with every test is that you can find an exception that makes the application ridiculous."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Srinivasan",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1107",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b7e294161f418f27706ae8c5baec0cd128fbba91ea099c85a350a6bee97a05f2",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b7e294161f41-0001-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 21,
        "start": 21
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. SRINIVASAN: Well, they -- they do in the following sense, Your Honor. For example, with the 10-K report for publicly traded companies, I think the question that is asked is not the location of the headquarters but the location of the principal executive offices. And so I think, by definition, in answering that question the principal executives would be located at that -- at that location."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1107",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b7e294161f418f27706ae8c5baec0cd128fbba91ea099c85a350a6bee97a05f2",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b7e294161f41-0001-0003",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 29,
        "start": 29
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "ORAL ARGUMENT OF TODD M. SCHNEIDER ON BEHALF OF THE RESPONDENTS"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Schneider",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1107",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b7e294161f418f27706ae8c5baec0cd128fbba91ea099c85a350a6bee97a05f2",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b7e294161f41-0001-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 30,
        "start": 30
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. SCHNEIDER: The -- the Ninth Circuit specifically in this case noted that 43 percent more employees for Hertz are in California, 75 percent more property, 60 percent more revenue, and --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1107",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b7e294161f418f27706ae8c5baec0cd128fbba91ea099c85a350a6bee97a05f2",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b7e294161f41-0001-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 31,
        "start": 31
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: Why -- why didn't they say place of doing business? That's not the terminology that they used."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Schneider",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1107",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b7e294161f418f27706ae8c5baec0cd128fbba91ea099c85a350a6bee97a05f2",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b7e294161f41-0002-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 38,
        "start": 38
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Congress had two goals,"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Schneider",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1107",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b7e294161f418f27706ae8c5baec0cd128fbba91ea099c85a350a6bee97a05f2",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b7e294161f41-0002-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 39,
        "start": 39
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The first goal was to prevent gaming of the system."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1107",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b7e294161f418f27706ae8c5baec0cd128fbba91ea099c85a350a6bee97a05f2",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b7e294161f41-0002-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 44,
        "start": 44
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Where is -- under the Ninth Circuit test, where is -- what is the principal place of business of Starbucks?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1107",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b7e294161f418f27706ae8c5baec0cd128fbba91ea099c85a350a6bee97a05f2",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b7e294161f41-0002-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 45,
        "start": 45
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Where is -- where is its headquarters."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1107",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b7e294161f418f27706ae8c5baec0cd128fbba91ea099c85a350a6bee97a05f2",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b7e294161f41-0002-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 46,
        "start": 46
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "What about, I guess, mail order houses? I mean, what's the principal place of business of Eddie Bauer?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1107",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b7e294161f418f27706ae8c5baec0cd128fbba91ea099c85a350a6bee97a05f2",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b7e294161f41-0002-0006",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 48,
        "start": 48
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The case is submitted."
    },
